course: dictionary
lesson: 3949
title: Words for saying goodbye
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A funeral is a ceremony held after someone dies. Family and friends gather to say goodbye and remember the person. Look at the words around it: «We wore dark clothes to the funeral, and nobody spoke loudly.» Dark clothes and quiet voices tell you it is a serious, respectful occasion.
explain: The word can also come before another word, as in «funeral service» or «funeral home». Here funeral describes the service or the home. To check, swap in a meaning: a service for a funeral still makes sense.
explain: Funerals are different in different families, religions and countries. «In a tangihanga, the body is not left alone, and people sing and give speeches.» So a funeral in one place may look very different from one in another, and we should always be respectful.
fact: A funeral is a ceremony held after someone dies.
fact: At a funeral, family and friends say goodbye and remember the person.
fact: «Funeral» can be a noun, as in «a funeral», or an adjective, as in «funeral service».
fact: A tangihanga is a Māori funeral, often held on a marae (a Māori meeting place) over about three days.
fact: Customs differ between cultures, so if you are not sure what to do at a funeral, ask a grown-up first.
exercise: What is a funeral? | A party to celebrate a birthday | A type of dance | *A ceremony held after someone dies, when family and friends say goodbye | A holiday at the seaside
exercise: In «funeral service», what kind of word is funeral? | *An adjective, describing the service | A noun, the name of a thing | A verb, an action word | A question word
exercise: «Chatting at a funeral can spoil things for others.» What should you do at a funeral? | Shout and laugh with your friends | *Be quiet and respectful | Run around the room | Eat your lunch as loudly as you can
test: At the end of a funeral, what happens to the body? | Nothing, it is taken home | It is put on a train | *It is buried or cremated | It is moved to a museum
test: Why might people smile at a funeral? | Because it is a rule to laugh loudly | Because nobody is allowed to cry | *To share happy memories of the person | To show they are bored
exam: Which sentence uses funeral as an adjective? | «He went to the funeral.» | «The funeral was on Monday.» | «Her funeral was sad.» | *«The funeral service was held in the church.»
